    "carers_allowance_earnings_taper": {
      "description": "Candidate measure. From 2030-31 Carer's Allowance no longer stops when weekly net earnings pass the £204 earnings limit (16 hours at the National Living Wage in 2026-27, held at £204 in the model): it is reduced by £1 for each £1 of weekly earnings above the limit, a 100% taper, to nothing once earnings exceed the limit by the full weekly rate. The government says the taper begins within 2030-31, once DWP's new IT system is ready; the model applies it to the whole of 2030-31. Carers at or below the limit are unchanged. Scotland's Carer Support Payment is unchanged. Claims by carers the limit kept out follow the data's take-up draw (60%). For a carer on Universal Credit the model counts the extra allowance in full as unearned income but deducts none of the PAYE on it from earnings, as DWP would, so such a carer can lose overall.",
      "display": "path",
      "rows": [
        {
          "label": "Weekly earnings at which Carer's Allowance stops",
          "unit": "gbp",
          "unit_words": "£ of net earnings a week",
          "primary": true,
          "points": [
